      "side": 1,
      "message": "After reading the spec again, I think this logic is incorrect here.  Your switch at line 482 is on the PD specification revision returned by the cable, but figure 5-1 indicates you should be checking the \"USB Highest Speed\" field from the Passive Cable VDO.\n\nYour check should be:\nswitch (cable[port].attr.p_rev30.ss)\n  default: /* not USB4 */\n  case USB_R30_SS_U40_GEN3: /* USB4 with USB4 Gen3 passive cable */\n  case USB_R30_SS_U32_U40_GEN1: /* USB4 with USB 3.2 Gen1 passive cable */\n  case USB_R30_SS_U32_U40_GEN2: /* Send SVID/Mode if board supports Gen3 */\n\nSo, the last case is the only time you\u0027ll move forward with the SVID SOP\u0027 and Mode SOP\u0027 messages to determine TBT support.\n\nAlso, since the Enter_USB message isn\u0027t supported by PD 2.0, you probably just want to disable USB4 if the cable\u0027s PD revision is 2.0.",
